{"qid":"Q756617","names":["Kingdom of Denmark"],"title":"Kingdom of Denmark","endonym":{"native":"Kongeriget Danmark","lang":"da"},"capsule":"The medieval Kingdom of Denmark coalesced under the Jelling dynasty in the 10th century, with Harald Bluetooth (r. c. 958–986) completing the Christianization of Denmark and unifying Jutland with the Danish islands. At its height under Valdemar II (r. 1202–1241), Denmark controlled the southern shores of the Baltic and much of the eastern coast, but the 1227 Battle of Bornhöved checked northward German expansion and reversed Danish Baltic dominance. The Kalmar Union (1397) brought Denmark, Norway, and Sweden under a single crown; rivalry with the Hanseatic League and internal Swedish opposition produced repeated crises until Sweden's permanent departure in 1523, leaving Denmark the dominant Scandinavian power.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Denmark's core territorial extent is well attested; the precise scope of overlordship over Schleswig, Holstein, and Baltic trading posts varied by period and is subject to ongoing historical interpretation.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Danish Realm","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Danish_Realm"},{"label":"Wikipedia: History of Denmark","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Denmark"}],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Danish Realm","rulers":[{"qid":"Q314490","name":"Gorm the Old","start":934,"end":958,"image":"Gorm-the-old.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Gorm-the-old.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"dllu","attributionRequired":false},"nativeName":"Gorm den Gamle","nativeLang":"da"},{"qid":"Q5960270","name":"Canute Danaást","start":947,"end":962,"image":"Knud-Danaást - udsnit fra kunstbladet \"Thyre Dannebod grundlægger Dannevirke\" (farvelagt).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Knud-Dana%C3%A1st%20-%20udsnit%20fra%20kunstbladet%20%22Thyre%20Dannebod%20grundl%C3%A6gger%20Dannevirke%22%20(farvelagt).jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Lorenz Frølich","attributionRequired":false},"nativeName":"Knud Danaást","nativeLang":"da"},{"qid":"Q201041","name":"Harald Bluetooth","start":962,"end":985,"image":"Grab von Harald Blauzahn in Roskilde 200710251128 00002.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Grab%20von%20Harald%20Blauzahn%20in%20Roskilde%20200710251128%2000002.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","artist":"Thborchert at German Wikipedia","attributionRequired":true},"nativeName":"Harald Blåtand","nativeLang":"da"},{"qid":"Q181896","name":"Sweyn I of Denmark","start":986,"end":1014,"image":"Sweyn Forkbeard by L. Frølich (cropped).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Sweyn%20Forkbeard%20by%20L.%20Fr%C3%B8lich%20(cropped).jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Oleryhlolsson","attributionRequired":false},"nativeName":"Svend Tveskæg","nativeLang":"da"},{"qid":"Q318912","name":"Eric the Victorious","start":992,"end":993,"image":"MELLIN(1850) p1.264 ERIK SEGERSALL.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/MELLIN(1850)%20p1.264%20ERIK%20SEGERSALL.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":null,"attributionRequired":false},"nativeName":"Erik Sejrsæl","nativeLang":"da"},{"qid":"Q311011","name":"Harald II of Denmark","start":1014,"end":1018,"image":"Painting of Harald II of Denmark (ca. 1880).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Painting